# Reactive Spotify Visualizers Implementation Plan

The user reported that Spotify visualizers (other than the vinyl spin) are not truly reactive. Currently, the [SpotifyPlayer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/SpotifyPlayer.tsx) uses basic CSS animations (`bar-grow`, `ring-pulse`) with random or time-based variations, but they don't respond to the actual audio data from Spotify.

## Proposed Changes

### [Frontend Components]

#### [MODIFY] [SpotifyPlayer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/SpotifyPlayer.tsx)
- Implement a mechanism to fetch audio analysis data from Spotify for the current track.
- Create a reactive loop that updates the visualizers based on the track's tempo (BPM) or sections.
- Ensure visualizers reflect the "energy" of the track.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Play music and switch between visualizer modes.
- Observe if the bars/rings/waveform pulse in sync with the beat.
- Pause music and verify animations stop or settle.
